PodClipper uses Ultralytics YOLO for person detection. Credit to Ultralytics
and its contributors: https://github.com/ultralytics/ultralytics
Ultralytics code and model weights are offered under AGPL-3.0 or a separate
Enterprise license. PodClipper uses the AGPL-3.0 option.

Local face verification uses OpenCV Zoo's YuNet face detector (MIT, copyright
2020 Shiqi Yu) and SFace face recognition model (Apache-2.0; contributed by
Yaoyao Zhong, with OpenCV conversion by Chengrui Wang). Model files are fetched
from a pinned OpenCV Zoo revision, checked against SHA-256 hashes, and cached
alongside their upstream licenses. They are not bundled in the Python wheel.
https://github.com/opencv/opencv_zoo/tree/47534e27c9851bb1128ccc0102f1145e27f23f98/models/face_detection_yunet
https://github.com/opencv/opencv_zoo/tree/47534e27c9851bb1128ccc0102f1145e27f23f98/models/face_recognition_sface

